om that view  uh met with uh our uh leaders at tribal  games and uh they met up and eventually  they got together to sort of pitch  themselves to uh nickelodeon and we got  uh the extreme pleasure of making that  game so that's pretty much how it  happened yeah that's absolutely amazing  because again it was one of those things  it's very certain different it's just so  everything happens in in its perfect  time so tell me because as i was  watching and playing the game it is one  of those things where you look at the  game and the nostalgia comes rushing  back it does look like a very old-school  pixel art beautiful game how is it  modernized because i was saying the same  thing it's obviously when you look at  the old games it brings you back and it  makes you think that it's an old game  but it's not it has very modern  sensibilities so tell me in what way  does it have modern text abilities well  the main one is now the uh it's in  widescreen with  instead of being four three like you  know uh when it's four three the turtles  are taller like in the art of the arcade  game so the fact that it's widescreen  and also like all of the animators  worked on  the previous game were brilliant but  they have a whole lot of limitations  that we don't have we have more colors  we can have animations with more frames  and so that allows for the turtles to  have  to be more distinctive and also have  everyone have their own animations and  so part wise that's how we can uh  also because we don't have the  limitations like the backgrounds can be  this these lovingly like almost pixel  painted lush  environments instead of being tile sets  so that's how  and also again because we don't have the  same limitations we can also have like  unique enemy spawns like so the  characters can just like pop up uh from  a desk or part of the background at the  full circle attack so  we really have the technology to make  to add more to uh classic pixel art  styles which is something we do 